course: dictionary
lesson: 14834
title: Racial and fair treatment
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Racial is an adjective. It means to do with race, the old idea of grouping people by skin colour, family background or where their ancestors came from. «The class studied racial equality, the idea that everyone should have the same rights.» The phrase «racial equality» tells you the topic is fair treatment for people of every race.
explain: Racial also describes things that happen between groups people see as different races. «Racial discrimination» means treating people unfairly because of their race. The clues are in words like unfairly and wrong, so you can tell it is a bad thing. Ask yourself: what word would fit here, and does my meaning still make sense in the sentence?
explain: Scientists now say all humans belong to one species, and races are not clear biological groups. But racism and its harm are real. So when you meet racial in history lessons, remember that it describes how people have been treated, and why that treatment was unfair.
fact: Racial means to do with race.
fact: Racial equality means everyone has the same rights, whatever their race.
fact: «Racial discrimination» means treating people unfairly because of their race.
fact: «Racial justice» means fair and equal treatment for people of every race.
fact: Scientists say all humans are one species, and races are not clear biological groups.
exercise: «The class studied racial equality, the idea that everyone should have the same rights.» What does racial equality mean? | Only one race is allowed to vote | People being sorted by how tall they are | *Everyone having the same rights, whatever their race
exercise: «Racial discrimination is treating people unfairly because of their race, and it is wrong.» What does racial discrimination mean? | *Treating people unfairly because of their race | Being kind to everyone at the same time | Sharing lunch with a friend
exercise: Which word is the adjective in «racial justice»? | both words | justice | *racial
test: The word racial means: | To do with the weather, such as a rainy day | *To do with race, such as «racial equality» | To do with cooking food
test: «The school dealt with racial tension between two groups of pupils.» What does racial tension mean? | *Tension between groups that people see as different races | Feeling nervous before a test | A tight, stretched string
exam: «Laws were passed to end racial discrimination, so that everyone was treated fairly.» What is the author showing? | The laws were made to make some people unfair | *Unfair treatment because of race was wrong and had to stop | Race is about how fast you can run
